 "notes": "Utility tractor (old k1) kept, compact/sub-compact aliases moved to new kinds; the single production model M7-173 (Kubota, ~170 hp ag tractor) dropped under the scope rule and the kind re-sourced to Wikipedia 'Tractor'. Ranges come from the Kubota 2025 full-line brochure, Wikipedia John Deere tractors, a dealer page for the JD 1 Series, TractorData series lists (Mahindra, Kioti), LS Canada site, New Holland compact page and the MF GC1700 brochure. No independent test winner found (searches gave only forums). Left out for lack of a retrievable page: Massey Ferguson compact/utility series (1800M/2800M release blocked 403), Yanmar, Iseki and TYM ranges, Grillo and Pasquali walking-tractor models (Grillo site 503, forums 402); Honda tillers are rotary tillers, not PTO two-wheel tractors. Wikidata returned 429. Two-wheel 'm' entries are notable models from the Wikipedia article and Farm Show (BCS)."
}